course: dictionary
lesson: 1255
title: Burial and what it means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Burial is a noun, and its verb is bury. Its main meaning is putting a dead body in the ground or a grave. «In a burial the coffin is lowered into a grave in a cemetery or churchyard.» The clues are coffin, grave and cemetery, so burial must mean putting a body in the ground.
explain: Burial can also mean the whole ceremony, which is the same as a funeral. «Throwing a little soil on the coffin is an old way of taking part in the burial and saying goodbye.» The clues are taking part and saying goodbye, so here burial means the ceremony, not just the digging.
explain: The word can also mean putting something under the ground, like treasure or rubbish. Use the context to decide. «A little burial in the garden is a way for people to say goodbye and thank you.» The words goodbye and thank you show that this burial is a ceremony for an animal.
fact: Burial is a noun. Its verb is bury, and its past form is buried.
fact: «Burial» means putting a dead body in the ground or a grave.
fact: «Burial» can also mean a funeral, the ceremony when a dead person is buried.
fact: Burial ground, burial site and burial at sea are phrases you may meet in history lessons and stories.
fact: Burial is one of two main ways families care for a body. The other is cremation, where great heat turns the body to soft grey ashes.
exercise: «In a burial the coffin is lowered into a grave.» What does burial mean? | Digging a hole to plant a tree | Burning something very hot | *Putting a dead body in the ground or a grave | A party with music and food
exercise: «Throwing a little soil on the coffin is an old way of taking part in the burial and saying goodbye.» In this sentence, what does burial mean? | A kind of soil | A hole in the road | A place for keeping old tools | *A ceremony where a dead person is buried
exercise: Which word is the verb that goes with burial? | *bury | burial | burials | berry
test: What is a burial site? | *A place where a dead person is buried | A place where people hold a party | A type of seashell | A shop that sells soil
test: «Families care for the body in one of two main ways: burial or cremation.» Which way turns the body to ashes? | Burial | Burying a box of treasure | *Cremation | Lowering a coffin into a grave
exam: Which word is a noun in this sentence? «The burial was quiet and peaceful.» | quietly | bury | buried | *burial
